  "claim_short": "Full negative answer to Remark 3.13 of arXiv:2405.17122: a stationary measurable probability kernel with the prescribed barycenter need not be the disintegration of any factor map. For Gamma equal to Z/2 with uniform admissible measure and trivial actions, take X a singleton and Y a uniform two-point space; the unique stationary kernel has the required barycenter, but no factor X to Y exists. A stronger...",
